{
    "background_story": "Eugene was a quirky inventor who lived in a small workshop above his family's antique store. He spent most of his days tinkering with gadgets and machinery, often using unconventional materials to create innovative solutions. One day, while rummaging through the store's attic, Eugene stumbled upon an old bedspring. Inspiration struck, and he decided to repurpose the spring as a makeshift catapult. With some clever modifications, the bedspring catapult was born. Eugene's contraption quickly gained popularity among the local children, who would gather to watch him launch water balloons and other small objects across the town square. Though his invention never made him rich, Eugene's creativity and resourcefulness earned him a reputation as the town's most ingenious tinkerer.",
